535: bridge, gives \(H(e)=1\). Equations (SC.17)--(SC.18), after the actual
536: line and collar maps above, therefore give
537: \[
538:  A_{\rm Jin}(f)=1,\qquad [\Phi]=1\in\Theta_7\cong\mathbb Z/28.
539:                                                                \tag{SC.19}
540: \]
541: The second equality is the oriented Hopf transfer of P3F.22. For the
542: forward physical return \(\Phi\), P3F.24 gives the literal cut-and-paste
543: identification
544: \[
545:  M_\Phi\cong(S^1\times S^6)\mathbin{\#}\Sigma_1.
546:                                                                \tag{SC.20}
547: \]
548: Both spin structures have Eells--Kuiper invariant \(1/28\), whereas
549: both spin structures of the product have value zero. Orientation
550: reversal changes the sign and still does not give zero. Consequently
551: this mapping torus is not diffeomorphic to the product, even without
552: an orientation requirement.
553: 
554: The loop in (SC.19) is one positive \(\rho\)-loop. Since
555: \(a'(u_*)=1-2u_*^{-3}=3\), the equation \(a(u)=\rho^2\) makes it
556: exactly two positive turns of the original marked source coordinate
557: \(u-u_*\). The scalar and all finite-cap choices stay fixed.
558: 
559: There is also an obstruction to smooth descent of this entire closed
560: family. Let
561: \[
562:  p:D_\rho^*\longrightarrow D_a^*,\qquad a=\rho^2,
563:                                                                \tag{SC.21}
564: \]
565: with \(u\) the analytic inverse of \(a(u)\) near \(u_*\). An oriented
566: smooth sphere bundle on \(D_a^*\) is obtained by cutting an annulus
567: along a radial interval and gluing its ends by an orientation-preserving
568: diffeomorphism \(\Phi_a\). Pulling this exact clutch construction back
569: along (SC.21) concatenates two copies of the interval; its closing map
570: is \(\Phi_a^2\). A change of fibre marking conjugates this map.
571: In \(\pi_0\operatorname{Diff}^+(S^6)\cong\Theta_7\) conjugation is
572: trivial because the group is abelian. Therefore an oriented smooth
573: bundle isomorphism from the actual \(\rho\)-family to such a pullback
574: would imply
575: \[
576:                 1=[\Phi]=2[\Phi_a]\quad\hbox{in }\mathbb Z/28.
577:                                                                \tag{SC.22}
578: \]
579: Reduction modulo two contradicts (SC.22). Thus this particular full
580: \(\rho\)-family does not descend as an oriented smooth bundle through
581: (SC.21). This does not exclude all conceivable one-turn endpoint maps:
582: it excludes exactly those that would give a descent of this specified
583: closed family.
584: 
585: No value for a different toric fan or another source-moduli puncture
586: is assigned by this proof.
587: 
588: Exact symbolic identities and the integral plumbing certificate are
589: saved separately in `code/part3/source_cusp_trace.py` and its outputs.
590: 
